                <section id="implementation">
                    <h2>Technical Implementation</h2>
                    
                    <h3>Data Structure</h3>
                    <p>The system uses a hierarchical data structure:</p>
                    <div class="code-block">
// Primary data structure
let sliceFunctions = []; // 3D: [slice][channel][coefficients]

// Example structure:
sliceFunctions = [
    [ // Slice 0 (darkest pixels)
        [a0, a1, a2, ...], // Red channel coefficients
        [b0, b1, b2, ...], // Green channel coefficients
        [c0, c1, c2, ...]  // Blue channel coefficients
    ],
    // ... more slices
];
                    </div>
                    
                    <h3>Key Functions</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>decomposeIntoSlices()</code>: Separates image by luminance</li>
                        <li><code>fitPolynomial2D()</code>: Fits polynomial to sampled points</li>
                        <li><code>reconstructImage()</code>: Rebuilds image from functions</li>
                        <li><code>calculateErrors()</code>: Computes quality metrics</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h3>Performance Optimizations</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Progressive sampling based on density parameter</li>
                        <li>Normal equations for efficient least squares</li>
                        <li>Memoization of basis function evaluations</li>
                        <li>Parallel processing of color channels</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                
                <section id="performance">
                    <h2>Performance Metrics</h2>
                    
                    <h3>Compression Ratio</h3>
                    <p>Typically achieves 10:1 to 100:1 compression depending on parameters and image complexity.</p>
                    <div class="formula">
                        Compression Ratio = (Original Size) / (Coefficient Size)
                    </div>
                    
                    <h3>Quality Metrics</h3>
                    <p>PSNR values:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>30-35 dB: Good quality (minimal noticeable artifacts)</li>
                        <li>35-40 dB: High quality</li>
                        <li>40+ dB: Excellent quality</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h3>Processing Time</h3>
                    <p>For 256×256 images on modern browsers:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Quick presets: 100-300 ms</li>
                        <li>High quality presets: 500-1000 ms</li>
                        <li>Maximum settings: 1-2 seconds</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                
